Building `3 9 20 null null 15 7` with a queue:

| take from queue | next two tokens | children attached | queue after |
|---|---|---|---|
| 3 | 9, 20 | 3.left = 9, 3.right = 20 | 9 20 |
| 9 | null, null | — | 20 |
| 20 | 15, 7 | 20.left = 15, 20.right = 7 | 15 7 |

The tokens run out, so 15 and 7 are leaves. Depth = 3 (3 → 20 → 15).

```cpp
int depth(Node* node) {
    if (!node) return 0;
    return 1 + max(depth(node->left), depth(node->right));
}
```

Maximum path sum for `-10 9 20 null null 15 7`:

| node | left gain | right gain | path turning here | returns |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 9 | 0 | 0 | 9 | 9 |
| 15 | 0 | 0 | 15 | 15 |
| 7 | 0 | 0 | 7 | 7 |
| 20 | 15 | 7 | 20 + 15 + 7 = **42** | 20 + 15 = 35 |
| −10 | 9 | 35 | −10 + 9 + 35 = 34 | 25 |

The best is 42, turning at 20 — not through the root.

```cpp
long long best;
long long gain(Node* node) {
    if (!node) return 0;
    long long l = max(gain(node->left), 0LL), r = max(gain(node->right), 0LL);
    best = max(best, node->val + l + r);
    return node->val + max(l, r);   // only one side can continue upwards
}
```

Right side view of `1 2 3 null 5 null 4`:

| round | queue at start | size | processed | last of level |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | **1** |
| 2 | 2 3 | 2 | 2, 3 | **3** |
| 3 | 5 4 | 2 | 5, 4 | **4** |

Answer: `1 3 4`.

